class.description:
[NetwDatabase] lets multiple Networked objects like [NetwEntity] and [NetwTableHandle] store and retrieve their state from a durable backend. A [NetwDatabase] needs a [NetwDatabaseBackend] which implements the actual storage and retrieval.
A database holds records. A record is a [Dictionary] created from a [NetwSchema] that can represent a [NetwEntity], a [NetwTableHandle] or any type of tabular data, stored under a durable [StringName] id. A [NetwSchema] can be interpreted as the table definition or shape and records as rows in this table.
A database admits no work until its [method open] has settled. Await it before starting play.
[codeblock]
func _ready() -> void:
    Netw.configure_database(self, &"saves").backend(preload("res://filesystem_backend.tres"))

func start_game(slot: StringName) -> void:
    var db: NetwDatabase = Netw.database(self, &"saves")
    var error: Error = await db.open(slot).wait()
    if error != OK:
        show_load_error(error)
        return
    enter_game()
[/codeblock]
